      "body": "Dear Joe,\r\n\r\nthanks for your interest in ARX!\r\n\r\nIn theory, all methods implemented by the tool are relevant for implementing privacy protection as required by the GDPR.\r\n\r\nIn practice, the suitability of different methods (or combination of methods) heavily depends on context (i.e. use cases, types of data involved).\r\n\r\nConsequently, it is basically impossible to give general advice. Instead, methods need to be selected and implemented by experts in accordance with guidelines (see e.g. the ENISA \"Privacy and Data Protection by Design\" guideline). Its likely that multiple tools and methods are needed.\r\n\r\nI will close this issue now. Should you have further questions in this regard, please feel free to contact us at arx.deidentifier@gmail.com\r\n\r\nBest regards\r\nFabian",
